# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values.
# .env.local is git-ignored — never commit real credentials.
#
# On Netlify these are set in the site's build environment rather than here.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A VARIABLE
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_-prefixed variable into the client bundle at build
# time. It is not a runtime lookup and it is not private: the value ends up as
# a literal string in the JavaScript served to every visitor, and anyone can
# read it with View Source.
#
# So a VITE_ variable may only ever hold something that is safe to publish —
# a public key, a project URL, a public app id. A secret belongs in Supabase
# function secrets, where the Edge Functions read it server-side (see
# supabase/functions/send-push and recognize-meal for the pattern).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── REQUIRED ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without these two the app does not start. They were missing from this file
# entirely, so a new contributor who copied it got a dead app and a console
# error with nothing pointing at the cause.
#
# Both are safe to expose. The anon key is a public, RLS-scoped credential and
# is already baked into the production bundle by design — the tables are
# protected by row-level security, not by the key being secret.
#
# Find both at: Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=


# ── OPTIONAL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Web Push (PWA notifications) — PUBLIC key only. The private key lives in
# Supabase function secrets (see supabase/functions/send-push/index.ts).
# Generate the pair with:  npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
# Blank disables push and the Settings toggle hides itself.
VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=

# MapTiler API key — the vector basemap for cardio route maps
# (CardioDetailModal + Hub PostActivityBlock). Free tier: 100k tiles/month.
# Get one at https://www.maptiler.com/cloud/ (Account → Keys → Default API Key).
# Blank falls back to OpenFreeMap "liberty" tiles — also free, less detailed.
VITE_MAPTILER_KEY=

# Sentry DSN — error monitoring. A DSN is designed to be public (it only
# accepts writes), so this one is genuinely fine to ship.
# Blank disables Sentry reporting.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# Tenor API key — the GIF picker in Hub chat.
# Blank hides the GIF button.
VITE_TENOR_API_KEY=


# ── NO LONGER USED ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY — REMOVED (Aug 2026). Nothing reads it any more.
#
# It used to gate an LLM polish pass on AI Coach replies that called
# api.anthropic.com straight from the browser. Because of the inlining rule at
# the top of this file, setting it published your Anthropic key to every
# visitor as plain text in the bundle — and nothing warned you, the Coach just
# started working better. It was never set in production, but the code path
# existed, which is one careless deploy away from the same outcome.
#
# The Coach's language model now lives behind the `coach-chat` Edge Function,
# which holds the key server-side as ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (a Supabase secret, the
# same one recognize-meal uses) and caps each user at 20 messages a day via
# migration 305. There is nothing to set here. If you find this variable in a
# .env.local, delete the line — it does nothing.
